   "answer": "Based on the provided sources, the differences between a current profile and a target profile depend on the framework being used:\n\n- For the NIST CSF, a Current Profile specifies the Core outcomes that an organization is currently achieving (or attempting to achieve) and characterizes how or to what extent each outcome is being achieved [2]. In contrast, a Target Profile specifies the desired Core outcomes that an organization has selected and prioritized for achieving its cybersecurity risk management objectives [2][5].\n- For the AI RMF, a Current Profile indicates how AI is currently being managed and the related risks in terms of current outcomes [3]. In contrast, a Target Profile indicates the outcomes needed to achieve the desired or target AI risk management goals [3].",
