   "answer": "- A \"CSF Community Profile\" is defined as \"A baseline of CSF outcomes that is created and published to address shared interests and goals among a number of organizations\" [1][2].\n- A Community Profile is typically developed for a particular sector, subsector, technology, threat type, or other use case [1][3].\n- An organization can use a Community Profile as the basis for its own Target Profile [1][3][5].\n- Examples of Community Profiles can be found on the NIST CSF website [3].",
