   "answer": "The four types of reflection tokens used in SELF-RAG, along with their input, output, and definitions from Table 1 and the text, are:\n\n1. Retrieve (Retrieval-on-demand): Type Input: x / x, y; Type Output: {yes, no, continue}; Definition: Given an input and previous-step generation (if applicable), an LM determines whether the continuation requires factual grounding [1][2].\n2. ISREL: Type Input: x, d; Type Output: {relevant, irrelevant}; Definition: d provides useful information to solve x [1].\n3. ISSUP: Type Input: x, d, y; Type Output: {fully supported, partially supported, no support}; Definition: All of the verification-worthy statement in y is supported by d [1].\n4. ISUSE: Type Input: x, y; Type Output: {5, 4, 3, 2, 1}; Definition: y is a useful response to x [1]. (Note that the bottom three rows are three types of Critique tokens) [1].",
